  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-rider",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "rider.heartbank.ceo — rotation over liveness.\n\nWhose turn it is, never who is best: no rating, no acceptance score, and passing is free. The route is deleted when the code is entered.",
      "page": "page-4"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-admin",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "admin.heartbank.ceo — one screen per sidebar item.\n\nEvery screen prints its own refusals, because an admin console is where deleted gradients come back to life. Shops has no performance column; Recommendation has no per-shop dial.",
      "page": "page-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-store",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "<tag>.heartbank.ceo — a customer's whole visit, signed out the entire way.\n\nRead left to right: the ORDER of these boards is the argument. The checkout asks for nothing but the price. The thank comes after the coffee is in her hand, on its own screen, with no amount pre-selected — because asked any earlier it would be a term of the price rather than a gift.\n\nExactly one line carries the B-Tag badge: Last of the pot, which has no fixed price at all. That is what the mark means now.",
      "page": "page-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-root",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "heartbank.ceo — the root.\n\nWho HeartBank is → who's near you → open your own. The whole path a shop owner walks before they have a shop.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-counter",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -271,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "counter.heartbank.ceo — Kanghna and Reach, on a phone behind the counter.\n\nTWO QUEUES, the founder's rule: people who checked in are standing in the line and are served in arrival order; orders sent from elsewhere wait separately.\n\nTop row is the daily work. Bottom row is the owner's Shop tab, which staff do not have at all — settings split four ways so no single screen is a wall.",
      "page": "page-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-1",
      "x": 2516,
      "y": 2796,
      "w": 240,
      "text": "need left and right margins",
      "page": "page-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-gift",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3520,
      "w": 460,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "B-Gift℠ / B-ReGift℠ — one instrument, three stages.\n\nThe payer cannot use it. The re-giver cannot use it — there is no redeem control on that screen, absent rather than disabled. Only the person it is finally given to can.\n\nNothing anywhere counts down."
    }
  ],
